    "turns": [
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "研究者为什么需要「DBSCAN 密度聚类」？当时已有的方法究竟卡在了哪里？",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial-hook"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "许多聚类方法偏好圆形簇，并要求分析前指定簇数量。",
            "sourceIds": ["source-a-density-based-algorithm-for-discovering-clusters"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.historical-background"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "如果一个点在 epsilon 范围内有足够邻居，它就是核心点；簇通过密度可达链条扩展。 关键机制是基于 epsilon 与 MinPts 的密度可达，它把资料线索与可见的演示行为连接起来。",
            "sourceIds": ["source-a-density-based-algorithm-for-discovering-clusters"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.core-idea"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "专家通常把 DBSCAN 视为标准的基于密度聚类方法，尤其适用于空间数据和不规则簇形状。它的长期影响在于核心点、边界点和噪声点的语言让异常处理和任意形状簇变得实用。",
            "sourceIds": ["source-a-density-based-algorithm-for-discovering-clusters"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.long-term-legacy"
        },
